# Capture Qualification Procedure

Status: DONE
Milestone: M0 Procedure definition only
Dependencies: None
Execution status: NOT_STARTED

## Purpose

Produce evidence for one exact package/OS/product/backend configuration without overstating coverage.

## Inputs

Approved required matrix; package hash; clean synthetic desktop/note; independent recipient;
recording permission; actual app/backend versions; docs\QUALIFICATION.md scenario/result template.

## Procedure

1. Set the root proof/qualification task IN_PROGRESS and create a new exact-configuration result.
2. Start independent capture before app launch; establish an appropriate synthetic positive control.
3. Record native configuration and local visibility separately from shell/picker observations.
4. Run steady-state and C01-C14 scenarios with repeated transitions as specified in QUALIFICATION.md.
5. Inspect recipient live output and applicable recordings, including every captured transition frame.
6. Record decoded frame counts/gaps, artifacts/hashes, leaks/residue, and environment limitations.
7. Classify PASS/FAIL_CONTENT_LEAK/FAIL_ARTIFACT/BLOCKED/UNSUPPORTED; never fill missing evidence as PASS.
8. Update only the exact tested matrix rows and root task evidence; preserve older results as history.

## Stop conditions

Any content-leak frame, invalid positive control, unexplained frame gaps, missing independent
output, unavailable required account/hardware, or mismatch between tested and release package.
Use synthetic text only; stop real-note use on a failed required path.

## Tasks

- [x] Define controls, independent observations, transitions, evidence, and outcome semantics.
- [x] Reference the detailed qualification matrix and record template without inventing results.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Procedure distinguishes pixel exclusion from getter success, picker omission, and OCR misses.
- [x] Output is a versioned limited result, never universal certification.

